WHY AGPL AND NOT MIT
====================

This repository is a measured-findings corpus and a risk screener. Its value
is not the code — it is the conclusion that most high-yield opportunities fail
basic solvency checks, and the harness that proves it case by case.

AGPL keeps that conclusion attributable. If you run a modified version of this
screener as a network service, you must publish your changes, so the corpus
stays honest and forkable rather than being quietly re-badged.

If you want to use this commercially without the AGPL network clause, that is
available under a separate license. Open an issue to discuss.

